WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.871
You can just follow your "List" or check out
the "what's new" or "what's hot" tabs, or

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.260
you can dig a little deeper into the Netflix
archives to find some truly outstanding, under-the-radar

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:10.760
films.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.420
Here's a look at some of the best stuff to
add to your queue the next time you don't

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.420
know what to watch.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.480
The South Korean film industry is thriving,
and Revenger is one of their most bone-shattering

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.660
creative exports.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:27.240
Directed by Seung-Won Lee, Revenger focuses
on protagonist Kim Yul, who's sentenced to

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.800
life in prison on an island known only as
AP-101.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.010
The island is a dumping ground to keep the
most violent criminals away from society,

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.140
and supposedly impossible to escape from.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.059
But here's the twist: Yul isn't trying to
get out.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.699
He got himself thrown into AP-101 on purpose
to find the man responsible for the brutal

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.020
murders of his family and avenge their deaths.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.880
He quickly connects with other inmates who
were wrongfully sentenced and puts his investigative

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.440
skills, and his combat expertise, to good
use to complete his mission.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.980
The plot of Revenger is certainly predictable
enough to anyone who enjoys action films,

00:00:59.989 --> 00:01:03.820
but the fight scenes are packed with the kind
of choreography that will make you ask "Wait,

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.160
how did he do that?"

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.700
It's hard to take your eyes off the insanely
talented star, Bruce Khan, as he takes down

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.320
the bad guys one by one.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:17.460
Based on a true story, Solo was originally
released in Spain in August 2018, and now,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.900
Netflix is bringing it to international audiences.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.820
When Álvaro wakes up hungover and depressed
in his Jeep in the Canary Islands, all he

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.740
can think about is the fight he just had with
his girlfriend and his newfound discovery

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.080
that his close friend Nelo is leaving him
behind to move to Canada.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.420
He decides to grab his surfboard and catch
a few waves to get his mind off everything,

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:40.390
but on his way down to the beach, he falls
and slides down the cliffs into the water

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.180
crashing against the rocks below.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.820
He hits his head and begins hallucinating,
reflecting on his life and his relationships

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.360
as he struggles to keep breathing.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:54.330
In Solo, the gorgeous setting of the Canary
Islands suddenly becomes foreboding and dangerous.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.960
Solo is the kind of film that prompts you
to consider what would run through your mind

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.160
if you were fighting for survival it's not
an easy watch, but one that will stay with

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:02.660
you.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:09.860
Not only is Lionheart the first Nigerian Netflix
original, it's also Nigerian superstar Genevieve

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:14.530
Nnaji's directorial debut and she just so
happens to be the star of the film as well,

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.340
putting her talents on full display.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:21.439
When her father has to step back from running
his transport company because of medical issues,

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.960
his daughter Adaeze decides she's ready to
take on the challenge.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.300
And appoints her uncle Godswill, who proves
tough to work with.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:32.520
When Adaeze and Godswill discover that the
company's finances are in shambles…

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:37.480
"Given our current situation… can you tell
us how bad the numbers are?"

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.760
“Bad. ... try abysmal, madam."

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.480
… they're forced to set their differences
aside and cooperate in order to save the business.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.660
This lighthearted family drama serves up more
than a few laughs and a strong feminist message.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.780
Kingdom is another solid Netflix original
out of South Korea, adapted from the webcomic

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.500
series Kingdom of the Gods.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:03.060
This genre-bending series pulls its inspiration
from both historical fiction and creepy zombie

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.620
flicks to create a fresh and exciting storyline.

00:03:06.049 --> 00:03:11.040
When a dead king comes back to life, his resurrection
seems to be the catalyst for a plague of mysterious

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:11.600
origins.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.060
In order to save the kingdom, the crown prince
must accept that the fight for their survival

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.600
is now his burden to bear.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:22.860
Royal politics and supernatural threats both
vie for center stage in this visually stunning

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.920
With only six episodes, Kingdom is easy to
watch in a single weekend which is ideal,

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.840
because once you hit play, you won't want
to get up until you watch the season finale.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:36.060
And here's the good news: season 2 started
production in early 2019.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.680
Close is based on the life of famous bodyguard
Jacquie Davis, who once worked for none other

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.790
than Harry Potter author J.K.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.300
Rowling.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:49.920
Directed by Vicky Jewson, the film stars Noomi
Rapace as Sam, a highly skilled bodyguard

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.960
who can make it out of any dangerous situation
unscathed.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:57.920
Sam ends up being assigned to protect spoiled
and naive teenage heiress Zoe Tanner, who

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.020
is set to inherit the wealth from her father's
mining company.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.840
"Take him to the kitchen … he needs to be
fed.”

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:06.800
“We leave in an hour.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:08.760
you might want to change."

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.890
The two head to Morocco, where Zoe will supposedly
be staying at a high-security compound to

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:17.180
ensure her safety but they quickly find themselves
under attack.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:22.080
Sam decides that being a protector isn't enough
it's her responsibility to teach Zoe how to

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:25.060
fight back and figure out exactly who's coming
after her.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:29.760
Rapace steals the show in this film she's
a tough protagonist with a tender side.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:34.510
While this high-stakes drama has been criticized
for a messy third act, it's entertaining enough

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.520
to invest 90 minutes of your time.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.820
Directed by Steven Soderbergh, the sports
drama High Flying Bird is unique in both plot

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:42.580
and production.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.520
For starters, it was shot entirely on an iPhone.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:50.550
During a pro basketball lockout, rookie player
Erick Scott wonders if his career has already

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:55.120
hit a dead end, until Ray Burke suggests an
unorthodox business model that could revive

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.440
the sport and disrupt the entire industry.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.880
Instead of relying on the wealthy team owners
to cave and end the stalemate, why not let

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.850
the players themselves take the reins and
run their own league, leveraging the internet

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.300
to independently broadcast games to millions?

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.460
"What you saw yesterday was just a glimmer.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.090
A lightning flash"

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:17.080
"What could be the beginning of a whole new
industry."

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.780
The economic critique at the core of the film
takes High Flying Bird outside the realm of

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.120
traditional sports movies.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.300
The biting commentary on the racial and class
dynamics within the world of professional

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:32.040
sports are apparent in real life, yet these
issues are often ignored by casual fans.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:36.860
It's easy to see pro athletes as privileged,
but High Flying Bird questions the power structure

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:41.590
integral to this industry when the owners
reap profits off the athletes who put in years

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.940
of hard work, who really comes out on top?

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:49.920
Equal parts buddy comedy and moving tearjerker,
Paddleton begins with the diagnosis of a terminal

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:54.229
illness… but it's not an inspirational film
about beating a disease and going on to live

00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:55.000
a happy life.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.020
When Michael finds out that he has stomach
cancer, which his doctor deems incurable,

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:01.200
he has no interest in proving her wrong.

00:06:01.389 --> 00:06:05.520
Instead, he decides that he wants to die on
his own terms, with the company of his neighbor

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.280
and only real friend, Andy.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:12.180
Mark doesn't have any major bucket list items
to check off there is no dramatic leap out

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.480
of a plane, no declarations of love to a long-lost
ex.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:20.220
Instead, Mark wants pizza nights complete
with corny kung-fu films and then re-enact

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:23.040
those corny kung fu films at an open mic night.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:31.600
"A great battle ensues and Lou winds up for
what will be known as the Death Punch."

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:36.640
He also wants to hang out with Andy and play
a few more rounds of Paddleton, a racquetball

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:37.840
game the pair invented.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:42.940
A film like Paddleton risks falling into feel-good
cliches familiar to this general narrative,

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.789
but the refreshingly authentic friendship
between these two misfits makes the movie

00:06:46.789 --> 00:06:49.260
something that goes far beyond the usual story.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:53.560
Mark doesn't harbor any illusions about a
miraculous recovery or a triumph over the

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:54.140
impossible.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:58.460
To journey through the quiet acceptance of
his own fate, he only needs the companionship

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.320
of a true friend.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:04.020
It's a reminder that meaning isn't always
found in grand, sweeping moments, but in the

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:05.250
connections with those we love.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:11.539
You're probably already familiar with Chiwetel
Ejiofor's from his work as an actor, an impressive

00:07:11.539 --> 00:07:15.919
filmography that includes prestigious dramas
like Children of Men and blockbusters like

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:16.900
Doctor Strange.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:21.820
Not only does The Boy Who Harnessed the Wind
mark his feature directorial debut, he also

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:24.940
wrote the script and appears as the father
of the young protagonist.

00:07:25.129 --> 00:07:29.800
The film is based on the real life of William
Kamkwamba and the memoir that detailed his

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:33.600
incredible achievements as a young boy growing
up in a small village in Malawi.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:38.520
Curious and inventive, William is barred from
attending school when his parents can no longer

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.380
pay the fees.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:44.000
His science teacher, however, continues teaching
him and allowing him to use the library.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:48.740
When his village suffers from a long drought
that results in famine, William must put his

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:52.539
skills to good use to create a windmill that
will power an electric water pump.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.840
There are no surprising twists or turns.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:58.820
It's a straightforward story that leads to
a conclusion you'll probably see coming, but

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:02.120
William's real life grit and ingenuity are
truly inspiring.

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:07.800
If you're looking for another unsettling sci-fi
series in with the same feel as Black Mirror,

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.800
Osmosis will be right up your alley.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:14.500
This French series explores a future in which
people can use an innovative new dating app

00:08:14.509 --> 00:08:18.080
to find their soulmate but it's not as simple
as swiping right.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.960
Instead, this service mines data from the
user's brain.

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:24.220
On the surface, it actually seems pretty innocent
at first.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:28.719
After all, if you could find "the one" with
perfect accuracy, without having to navigate

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:32.920
the complicated landscape of modern dating,
you'd probably be tempted to give it a shot.

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:35.920
But naturally, there are some unintended consequences.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:40.660
As the developers behind the service warn
the participants, every experiment has a margin

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:41.220
of error.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:45.860
While the idea behind the series isn't exactly
groundbreaking, the story itself is engaging

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:51.230
and suspenseful, and the futurist virtual
reality sequences make for some unique cinematography.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:57.310
When it comes to sheer intensity, Black Summer
is a step up from classic zombie films.

00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:59.940
In this series, the undead aren't lumbering
around aimlessly.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:03.220
They're fast, they're hungry, and they're
downright terrifying.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:08.130
In the days following the onset of a zombie
apocalypse, a group of desperate strangers

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:12.530
bands together, hoping that strength in numbers
will increase their chances of survival.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:16.480
Sure, it sounds like the beginning of any
story about the collapse of society, but Black

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:20.480
Summer is relentless in showcasing the full
extent of the ensuing violence.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:23.780
The characters don't get a moment to breathe,
and neither does the viewer.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.900
Be prepared for nauseating gore and plenty
of jump scares.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:32.760
Even if you only skimmed Lord of the Flies
in high school, you probably remember the

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:37.200
basic plot: a group of boys get stranded on
an island and attempt to organize their own

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:42.300
mini-society until help arrives, but it devolves
into chaos and tragedy ensues.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:47.160
That's also the general storyline in the series
The Society, but this modern take on the dilemma

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:51.700
from the classic novel doesn't feel like a
mere rehash with electricity and iPhones.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:55.940
When students return from a school trip to
find that everyone in their town has vanished

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:59.980
and the community is now surrounded by an
impenetrable forest, they quickly realize

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:02.180
that they're ill-equipped to handle what comes
next.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:03.100
"It's nonsense."

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.900
"It’s Hebrew, it means you have been weighed
in the balance and found wanting."

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:11.620
Although teenagers are the audience most likely
to find the characters relatable, you don't

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:16.579
have to be a high school student to appreciate
the ensemble cast and realistic take on adolescent

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.960
conflict against an apocalyptic backdrop.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:23.280
From the first episode, viewers are sure to
find themselves gripped by the mystery is

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:28.180
the town at the center of some grand experiment,
or have they slipped into a parallel universe?

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:29.440
Is help on the way?

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:32.040
And if it arrives, will it be too late?

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.420
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:38.660
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:42.420
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

